  <encodingDesc>
    <projectDesc>
      <p>The Electronic Corpus of 17th- and 18th-century Polish Texts, also known as KorBa (an acronym of Korpus Barokowy, which is Polish for The Baroque Corpus), is the primary result of two projects carried out in the years 2013-2018 and 2018-2023 by the Department of the History of the 17th and 18th Century Polish of the Institute of Polish Language, Polish Academy of Sciences (PAS), in cooperation with the Linguistic Engineering Group of the Institute of Computer Science, Polish Academy of Sciences.</p>
      <p>The presented subcorpus consists of c. 850 thousand tokens as understood by the creators of the National Corpus of Polish. It contains samples from all of the texts included in the full corpus. The majority of samples has been annotated manually by two independent annotators (in the second stage of the project - by the annotator and the tagger) and the conflicts between their decisions were resolved by an adjudicator. A part of the samples has been processed by a single annotator. These samples have symbol "_s" attached to the ID. The texts are presented in both transcribed and transliterated forms.</p>
      <p>The corpus was created in cooperation with Linguistic Engineering Group (Institute of Computer Science, Polish Academy of Sciences).</p>
      <p>More information about the corpus can be found at https://www.korba.edu.pl/ tab About the Corpus.</p>
    </projectDesc>
